    purpose: "Where a voltage source holds voltage constant, a current source holds current constant: connect any load and it adjusts its output voltage so that exactly, say, 20 mA flows. That suits driving LEDs (their brightness depends on current), charging batteries, exciting sensors such as thermistors and RTDs, and modelling photodiodes and transistor outputs in simulation. In this app the DC current source is ideal, and current flows out of its out pin. In hardware, current sources are built from a transistor, an op-amp, a regulator such as the LM317 plus a resistor, or a dedicated LED driver chip.",
