    purpose: "A Zener diode conducts normally in the forward direction, but its real job is in reverse: it blocks until the voltage reaches its Zener voltage, then conducts as much as needed to hold the voltage there. That makes it a simple reference or small regulator, and a clamp that protects inputs and MOSFET gates from overvoltage. Values run from about 2.4 V to over 100 V. Examples: 1N4728A (3.3 V), 1N4733A (5.1 V), 1N4740A (10 V), 1N4742A (12 V), 1N4744A (15 V) and 1N4750A (27 V), all 1 W, plus the BZX55C3V3 (3.3 V, 0.5 W).",
