    summary: "A sturdy clamping diode that absorbs brief voltage spikes from static, surges and inductive kicks before they reach sensitive parts.",
    purpose: "A transient voltage suppressor (TVS) is a diode built to survive large, brief bursts of energy. It sits across a power or signal line and does nothing in normal operation, but when a spike pushes the voltage too high (static from a finger, a car's load dump, interference picked up by a long cable, a motor's kick) it conducts heavily and clamps it. Unidirectional types such as the SMAJ5.0A suit DC lines; bidirectional types, marked with a C as in SMBJ12CA, suit signals that swing both ways. The P6KE series is the classic through-hole family.",
