    purpose: "An N-channel MOSFET (metal-oxide-semiconductor field-effect transistor) is the go-to power switch: a voltage on its gate opens a path between drain and source whose resistance can be just a few milliohms, and the gate draws almost no steady current. Uses include switching motors, solenoids, LED strips and heaters from a microcontroller, switching regulators, motor drivers and level shifters. Small-signal parts: 2N7000 and BSS138 (about 200 mA), AO3400 (SOT-23, about 5 A). Logic-level power parts: IRLZ44N, IRLB8721. Standard-gate power parts needing about 10 V drive: IRFZ44N, IRF540N, IRF3205, IRFB4410, IRFP260N.",
